  "findings": [
    "Both themes retain the same option order, square letter boxes, legible text and spacing at the measured314 outer and312 media content widths. A/B/C show the expected Cover slices. D has no media frame or empty placeholder.",
    "Each settled A/B selected view has a filled, slightly rotated letter, accent rail and border, and a restrained themed header glow. The other visible letters remain outlined. The light post-Refresh original visibly retains the B selection and rendered photos.",
    "Both A viewer originals show the full portrait at initial100% with readable reset, help and close controls and no gallery navigation. The Native day percentage uses the user-approved light color."
  ],
  "visibleDifferences": [
    "Native paints the inset selection rail over the left thumbnail edge as well as the header. The Web image covers that part of the inset effect, so its thick rail is mainly visible in the header. The accent border and selected letter remain easy to distinguish on both.",
    "Native and Web render the selected header gradient and shadow with slightly different falloff. The closed Web reference also shows a pointer hover tint on A while B remains selected.",
    "Native originals include the system safe areas and the existing persistent gameplay header. Scroll framing, surrounding question decoration and the larger Native submit button are outside this choice component review."
  ],
